## Authorized File Download Pattern

```java
@GetMapping("/api/files/{fileId}/download")
public ResponseEntity<String> getDownloadUrl(
        @PathVariable Long fileId,
        @AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails user) {

    FileRecord file = fileRepo.findById(fileId).orElseThrow();

    // Authorization check — does this user own the file?
    if (!file.getOwnerId().equals(user.getId())) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(403).build();
    }

    // Generate 10-minute presigned URL
    String url = storageService.generatePresignedDownloadUrl(
        file.getS3Key(), Duration.ofMinutes(10)
    );

    return ResponseEntity.ok(url);
    // Client uses this URL to download directly from S3
}
```

## Simple Multipart Upload

```java
@Service
public class LargeFileUploadService {
    private final S3TransferManager transferManager;
    private final String bucketName;

    public LargeFileUploadService(S3Client s3Client,
                                   @Value("${aws.s3.bucket}") String bucket) {
        this.transferManager = S3TransferManager.builder()
            .s3Client(s3Client)
            .build();
        this.bucketName = bucket;
    }

    public String uploadLargeFile(Path filePath, String key) {
        FileUpload upload = transferManager.uploadFile(b -> b
            .putObjectRequest(r -> r.bucket(bucketName).key(key))
            .source(filePath)
        );

        CompletedFileUpload result = upload.completionFuture().join();
        return result.response().eTag();
        // TransferManager automatically uses multipart for files > threshold
    }

    public void downloadLargeFile(String key, Path destination) {
        FileDownload download = transferManager.downloadFile(b -> b
            .getObjectRequest(r -> r.bucket(bucketName).key(key))
            .destination(destination)
        );
        download.completionFuture().join();
    }
}
```

## Browser Direct Upload with Presigned Multipart

```java
// Step 1: Initiate multipart upload
@PostMapping("/api/uploads/initiate")
public InitiateUploadResponse initiateUpload(@RequestBody UploadRequest req) {
    CreateMultipartUploadResponse response = s3Client.createMultipartUpload(b -> b
        .bucket(bucketName)
        .key("uploads/" + UUID.randomUUID() + "/" + req.getFilename())
    );
    return new InitiateUploadResponse(response.uploadId(), response.key());
}

// Step 2: Generate presigned URL for each part
@PostMapping("/api/uploads/{uploadId}/parts")
public UploadPartUrlResponse getPartUrl(
        @PathVariable String uploadId,
        @RequestParam String key,
        @RequestParam int partNumber) {
    // partNumber: 1 to 10000
    try (S3Presigner presigner = S3Presigner.builder().build()) {
        String url = presigner.presignUploadPart(b -> b
            .signatureDuration(Duration.ofHours(1))
            .uploadPartRequest(r -> r
                .bucket(bucketName)
                .key(key)
                .uploadId(uploadId)
                .partNumber(partNumber))
        ).url().toString();
        return new UploadPartUrlResponse(url, partNumber);
    }
}

// Step 3: Complete upload after all parts uploaded
@PostMapping("/api/uploads/{uploadId}/complete")
public String completeUpload(@PathVariable String uploadId,
                              @RequestBody CompleteUploadRequest req) {
    List<CompletedPart> parts = req.getParts().stream()
        .map(p -> CompletedPart.builder().partNumber(p.getPartNumber()).eTag(p.getEtag()).build())
        .toList();

    s3Client.completeMultipartUpload(b -> b
        .bucket(bucketName)
        .key(req.getKey())
        .uploadId(uploadId)
        .multipartUpload(m -> m.parts(parts))
    );
    return "https://" + bucketName + ".s3.amazonaws.com/" + req.getKey();
}
```

## Cleanup Lifecycle Rule

```bash
# Abort incomplete multipart uploads after 7 days
aws s3api put-bucket-lifecycle-configuration \
  --bucket my-app-uploads \
  --lifecycle-configuration '{
    "Rules": [{
      "Id": "CleanIncompleteMultipart",
      "Status": "Enabled",
      "AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload": {"DaysAfterInitiation": 7}
    }]
  }'
```

## Architecture: S3 → SQS → Spring Boot

```
User uploads CSV
    ↓
[S3 Bucket: uploads/] ─── ObjectCreated event
    ↓
[SQS Queue: file-processing-queue]
    ↓
[Spring Boot Consumer]
    ├── Download from S3
    ├── Parse CSV
    └── Save to DB
```

