## Spring Boot S3 Event Consumer

```java
@Value
public static class S3EventMessage {
    String bucket;
    String key;
    String eventTime;
}

@Service
public class FileProcessingConsumer {
    private final S3Client s3Client;
    private final CsvProcessingService csvService;
    private final ProcessedFileRepository processedFileRepo;

    @SqsListener("file-processing-queue")
    public void handleFileUpload(String rawMessage) throws Exception {
        // Parse S3 event message
        JsonNode root = objectMapper.readTree(rawMessage);
        JsonNode record = root.path("Records").get(0);

        String bucket = record.path("s3").path("bucket").path("name").asText();
        String key = URLDecoder.decode(
            record.path("s3").path("object").path("key").asText(), "UTF-8");

        // Idempotency check
        if (processedFileRepo.existsByBucketAndKey(bucket, key)) {
            log.info("Already processed: {}/{}, skipping", bucket, key);
            return;
        }

        // Download and process
        byte[] content = s3Client.getObjectAsBytes(
            r -> r.bucket(bucket).key(key)
        ).asByteArray();

        csvService.importCsv(new ByteArrayInputStream(content));

        // Mark as processed (idempotency record)
        processedFileRepo.save(new ProcessedFile(bucket, key, Instant.now()));
        log.info("Processed file: {}/{}", bucket, key);
    }
}
```

## Upload Flow

```
1. Browser: POST /api/uploads/request-url
   { filename: "avatar.jpg", contentType: "image/jpeg" }

2. Backend: generate pre-signed PUT URL for S3
   → returns: { uploadUrl: "https://bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/uuid.jpg?X-Amz-Signature=...",
                key: "uploads/uuid.jpg" }

3. Browser: PUT https://bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/uuid.jpg?X-Amz-Signature=...
   (request goes directly to S3, bypassing your server)

4. Browser: POST /api/uploads/confirm { key: "uploads/uuid.jpg" }
   (tell backend the upload is complete)

5. Backend: validate key, update user profile with avatar URL
```

## Spring Boot Implementation

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/uploads")
public class UploadController {

    private final S3Presigner presigner;
    private final String bucketName;

    @PostMapping("/request-url")
    public PresignedUploadResponse requestUploadUrl(
            @RequestBody UploadRequest req,
            @AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt) {

        // Generate unique key with user prefix (limits what user can overwrite)
        String key = "user-uploads/" + jwt.getSubject() + "/" +
                     UUID.randomUUID() + "-" + req.filename();

        // Pre-sign PUT request — valid for 10 minutes
        PutObjectPresignRequest presignRequest = PutObjectPresignRequest.builder()
            .signatureDuration(Duration.ofMinutes(10))
            .putObjectRequest(PutObjectRequest.builder()
                .bucket(bucketName)
                .key(key)
                .contentType(req.contentType())  // enforce content type
                .contentLength(req.fileSizeBytes())
                .build())
            .build();

        PresignedPutObjectRequest presigned = presigner.presignPutObject(presignRequest);

        return new PresignedUploadResponse(
            presigned.url().toString(),
            key,
            Duration.ofMinutes(10).toSeconds()
        );
    }
}
```

